    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0490" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/796: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-10T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 10—11:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>984. 1. On October 17, the Senior Minister informed the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs that the diplomatic body agreed to the continuation in Peking of the
                    work of the Tariff Valuation Revision Commission.</p>
                <p>2. The Minister of Foreign Affairs has now notified this Legation the next
                    Commission will convene here on December 1st.</p>
                <p>3. Commercial attaché suggests that the Department request the Treasury to
                    instruct Nicholson<anchor n="56" xml:id="d362-f1"/> to proceed to Peking for
                    this purpose. I concur.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d362-f1" n="56" xml:id="d362-f1-content">
                <p>Martin R. Nicholson, Treasury representative at Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
